  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.58,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J12"],
      "pins": ["J12.1", "J12.2", "U8.13", "U2.1", "U2.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/Microcontroller/NET0003"],
      "observed": "The netlist contains an additional 2-pin screw terminal, J12, with pin 1 tied to GND and pin 2 tied to /Microcontroller/NET0003. That same net is the heater-control node: ESP32 GPIO1 (U8 pin 13) and the TPS1H200 high-side-switch IN/DIAG_EN pins (U2 pins 1 and 2).",
      "expected": "The specification describes the heater control path as firmware-driven from ESP32 GPIO1 into the TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN pins, with no user-accessible screw terminal or external override on that control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"J12\") (value \"Screw_Terminal_01x02\") (footprint \"TerminalBlock_4Ucon:TerminalBlock_4Ucon_1x02_P3.50mm_Horizontal\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"5\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0003\") (node (ref \"D7\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"J12\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"13\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J12\") (pin \"1\") ...) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Drives a single heater output net through a smart high-side switch (U6, TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1), switched from the ESP32's GPIO1"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A wire, jumper, or conductive object placed across J12 can pull the heater-control GPIO low or inject an external voltage into the MCU GPIO and high-side-switch input. This bypasses the intended firmware-only heater control and can damage the ESP32 GPIO, changing the board's safety and control behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files match the specified power, SPI, thermocouple, fan, and heater-switch topology, but they include an undocumented screw terminal connected directly to the ESP32 GPIO1/heater-control net, which creates an external override/short path not present in the intended design."
}

